From aea8d4e339f1eaf1686b90ba82b8873e5445282f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 20:35:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] icu74: our own build, with the data in the library

The arm64 list took the bootstrap icu74 from the package server, and the
bootstrap libicudata.so is a stub that loads icudt74l.dat at run time --
which nothing on Haiku points at (upstream Haiku links ICU into libbe and
never runs the stub). Every ICU-backed format in the system came out
empty: BNumberFormat::Format() failed, string_for_size() printed the unit
with no number, and ActivityMonitor said "Used memory -- MiB" about a
kernel that knew perfectly well (get_system_info() answered a probe with
the right numbers all along).

prosepkg builds icu74 74.1-6 from the community's recipe with two
changes (packages/builder/overlay/dev-libs/icu): the data is linked into
libicudata.so (--with-data-packaging=dll, ~30 MB, no path to find and no
environment to set), and the tools the build runs over the data are
built natively on the Mac first (--with-cross-build, ICU's own recipe
for cross-building).

The names the build resolves are unchanged (icu74, icu74_devel,
icu74_tools), so BuildFeatures and the profiles see the same things;
only the version moves. local-packages.sh picks the new files up like
any other package the fork lists beyond upstream's.

Verified on the dev machine: with this package in place of the bootstrap
one, BNumberFormat and BStringFormat succeed with no ICU_DATA set, and
ActivityMonitor's legend reads "Used memory 240 MiB, Cached memory
165 MiB".

